WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.744
By the end of the Tang dynasty, the court was utterly corrupt; officials feasted all day while the people's lives grew harder and harder.

00:00:10.094 --> 00:00:14.006
The common people had no food to eat, and their hearts filled with resentment.

00:00:14.356 --> 00:00:23.020
A man named Huang Chao stood up and led everyone to take up arms and resist the corrupt court.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:29.586
The rebel army swept across the land like a tide, growing ever larger, a mighty and imposing force.

00:00:29.936 --> 00:00:34.760
They passed town after town, and the news spread everywhere.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:42.598
Very soon they fought their way into the capital, Chang'an, and rebel red flags flew from the city gate tower.

00:00:42.948 --> 00:00:51.612
Sadly, this great war gravely wounded the country: crops withered and died, and the people were displaced and homeless.

00:00:51.962 --> 00:00:58.610
As the sun set in the west, the once-glorious Tang dynasty stepped slowly toward decline.

